# [PROJECT NAME] Workflow Prompts

## Repository orientation

Read the applicable `AGENTS.md`, `GOALS.md`, `PLANS.md`, `PROMPTS.md`, `harness/build-log.md`, and relevant files under `harness/context/`. Perform a read-only discovery pass. Report the repository purpose, current state, constraints, available checks, and unknowns. Do not edit files.

## Phase preparation

Read the selected phase file under `harness/build/` and all referenced context. Summarize scope, exact files, acceptance criteria, risks, and non-goals. Record authorization already present in the request or selected workflow; ask only for a missing material decision. A planning-only request stops here. When the enclosing request also authorizes implementation, proceed within that scope.

## Execute one approved phase

Execute the authorized phase and any continuation explicitly included in the enclosing request. Follow red, green, refactor, and verification where appropriate. Run the repository's applicable checks. For dev-work/dev-push, scoped commit, push, and PR delivery follow the shared delivery contract without another approval gate. Do not infer merge, deployment, unrelated work, or publication authority for a local-only workflow.

## Verification and evidence

Inspect the final diff and repository status. Record exact commands and observed results in `harness/build-log.md`, linking private evidence without copying sensitive payloads. If a check fails, distinguish product defects from environment or runner-protocol failures before choosing a scoped correction; passing checks do not establish untested behavior.

## Review and remediation

Review only the selected scope. Prioritize correctness, security, data integrity, recovery behavior, and user-visible regressions. Cite exact files and lines. Implement scoped remediation when the enclosing request or dev-work already authorizes it; otherwise report findings and ask before repairs.

## Phase completion and handoff

Summarize the completed scope, changed files, tests, validation evidence and remaining risks. Stop at the requested boundary; continue to the next phase only when already included in the enclosing request.
